{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"QNet Ltd, formerly known as QuestNet, GoldQuest, and QI Limited, is a Hong Kong-based multi-level marketing (MLM) company owned by the QI Group.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The company sells a variety of products including energy, weight management, nutrition, personal care, home care, and fashion accessories etc. on an e-commerce platform.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" QNet was founded in Hong Kong by Vijay Eswaran in 1998 along with QN Europe and other companies.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Since it was first introduced in 1998, Qnet (doing business at the time as Questnet) promoted gold and silver coins with an MLM system.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" But the coin collection business was touted as a money game and declared illegal in some countries.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" A few years later Questnet came up with a new name, Qnet and offered various other products via the MLM system.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It promotes its products on its website using claims "that would not pass official muster in much of the world."","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Despite claiming to be an e-commerce based business, an ordinary retail customer can make a purchase of a product from the website only if they have a referrer ID of an independent representative of QNet.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" Unlike other e-commerce websites; purchases without this ID are not allowed.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" Qnet used websites/servers viz., www.qnetindia.in, www.qnetindia.net, www.qnet.net, www.questnet.net, to conduct its business which were blocked by Indian Computer emergency response team (CERT) following a court order.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" Other websites like portal.qnetindia.net, are being investigated by the government and further action on the websites have been promised after details are gathered.","title":"Qnet"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"GrocerKey is a Madison, Wisconsin company, founded in 2015, that creates e-commerce software for grocery stores to sell products online at their in-store prices.","title":"GrocerKey"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Customers can choose to pick up their groceries in the store or have them delivered that day, as long as they order before a certain time.","title":"GrocerKey"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The company does not charge fees up front to build the e-commerce platform; instead, the company generates revenue by charging grocers a fee (ranging from less than 1% to 12% on each transaction conducted through the online store depending on the level of service provided by GrocerKey on behalf of the retailer.)","title":"GrocerKey"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"DCKAP is an American and Indian firm that builds e-commerce store fronts for Magento, an open-source e-commerce platform, and is based in Fremont, California.","title":"DCKAP"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" DCKAP was founded in 2005 by Indian-American Karthik Chidambaram.","title":"DCKAP"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Souq.com is an English-Arabic language e-commerce platform, often described as the Amazon of the Middle East.","title":"Souq.com"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the largest e-commerce platform in the Arab world.","title":"Souq.com"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" On March 28, 2017, Amazon.com Inc. confirmed it would be acquiring Souq.com for $580 million.","title":"Souq.com"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Zilzar (Arabic: زلزار) is a privately held, online marketing platform headquartered in Malaysia, specifically catering to Muslim consumers seeking halal products and services.","title":"Zilzar"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The company positions itself as a global Muslim lifestyle marketplace where consumers can access information, content, community and trade.","title":"Zilzar"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" This e-commerce platform was launched in 2014 by Malaysian Prime Minister, Dato Sri Muhamad Najib Tun Razak in the 10th World Islamic Economic Forum in Dubai.","title":"Zilzar"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The site was described as a way of empowering the consumer and creating employment for Muslims in emerging markets by the country's prime minister.","title":"Zilzar"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The business describes its aim as connecting Muslim consumers and making it easier for halal traders around the world to conduct business online.","title":"Zilzar"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The platform handles content regarding Islamic societies and products that deals with the compliance of the Islamic Sharia law.","title":"Zilzar"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Buildabazaar.com is an e-commerce Saas platform built by Infibeam with operations in India and Middle East.","title":"Buildabazaar"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The technology infrastructure of infibeam.com was extended as an e-commerce platform and launched as buildabazaar in 2011.","title":"Buildabazaar"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is a self-service platform where users can create an e-commerce store, upload their product catalog, customize their site and sell their products.","title":"Buildabazaar"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Buildabazaar is offered as a SaaS platform for creating online retailing websites and travel booking sites.","title":"Buildabazaar"}],"peer_messages":[" A few years later Questnet came up with a new name, Qnet and offered various other products via the MLM system.","title":"Qnet"}
